As with https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/41165/files#r768565452, I'd argue the `nop` is better at mimicking the non-async behaviour. If not, then `onDestroy` should at least be called with `err`, instead of `null`:

```js
if (!called) {
  process.nextTick(onDestroy, null);
}
```

Anyway, that was before knowing about #40773.
